045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "71351b80-5668-5d34-aba6-344b6732f5d4" :question/math-academy-id "q-81205" :question/problem "If $U={-20,-18,-16,-14,…,20}$ is the universal set and $A={-20,-16,-12,-8,…,20},$ then $\\overset{―}{A}=$" :question/worked-solution "The complement of $A,$ denoted $\\overset{―}{A},$ consists of every element in the universal set $U$ that is not in the set $A.$\n\nThe universal set $U$ consists of the even integers $-20$ through $20,$ while the set $A$ consists of the multiples of $4$ from $-20$ through $20.$\n\nSo, the only elements of $U$ that are not in $A$ are the even integers from $-18$ through $18$ that are not multiples of $4.$\n\nTherefore, the complement of $A$ is\n\n$$\n\\overset{―}{A}={-18,-14,-10,-6,-2,2,6,10,14,18}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186371951 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "49251196-c06b-5718-82e6-5ed9450301af" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Complement of a Set Given Using Ellipsis Notation"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c9c67403-b4d7-5dbb-84e7-5fb2795f5c31" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{-75,-70,-65,…,25}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186371953} {:answer/id #uuid "92f6308e-0b2e-53ad-8dfa-9ad817647e78" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{-75,-65,-55,…,25}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186371954} {:answer/id #uuid "38a46be0-31f5-5e33-bfea-1b59bea9cd6b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{-75,-60,-45,…,25}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186371955} {:answer/id #uuid "cc9d30f3-3974-5658-a7ac-047c9bc91c36" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{-75,-65,-55,…,30}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186371956} {:answer/id #uuid "28c08420-cbfd-5b9f-8b54-131b89a64da5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{-75,-65,-55,…,35}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186371957}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "92f6308e-0b2e-53ad-8dfa-9ad817647e78" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{-75,-65,-55,…,25}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186371954} :answer-field/id #uuid "4ee85bb5-8edd-526c-806d-2b23dbc0f371" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186371952}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "579decd3-1e02-54bf-b9cc-2b261af84aae" :question/math-academy-id "q-81206" :question/problem "If $U={-80,-75,-70,…,30}$ is the universal set and $A={-80,-70,-60,…,30},$ then $\\overset{―}{A}=$" :question/worked-solution "The complement of $A,$ denoted $\\overset{―}{A},$ consists of every element in the universal set $U$ that is not in the set $A.$\n\nThe universal set $U$ consists of the multiples of $5$ from $-80$ through $30,$ while the set $A$ consists of the multiples of $10$ from $-80$ through $30.$\n\nSo, the only elements of $U$ that are not in $A$ are the multiples of $5$ from $-75$ through $25$ that are not multiples of $10.$\n\nTherefore, the complement of $A$ is\n\n$$\n\\overset{―}{A}={-75,-65,-55,…,25}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186371958 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "19fb3196-439e-5466-b50c-615c492167b4" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Complement of a Set Using a Venn Diagram"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e825fed4-4b50-5a5c-b86a-ec850528b53e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{1,2,a,d}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186371960} {:answer/id #uuid "f6e905fa-d7ee-5c6d-9ebc-27785976db0b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{1,2,3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186371961} {:answer/id #uuid "23ec1e0f-838c-5c61-a5ab-44bbaa4f6ce0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{a,b,c,d}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186371962} {:answer/id #uuid "5047d40b-e4e0-5d3c-9463-299472266d07" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{1,2,3,a}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186371963} {:answer/id #uuid "02d07d2a-3548-5e90-8f70-e700403d6b99" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{2,d}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186371964}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e825fed4-4b50-5a5c-b86a-ec850528b53e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{1,2,a,d}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186371960} :answer-field/id #uuid "0705b467-9e6b-530c-94d6-8ab2bb1f0319" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186371959}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "5719c33d-34a9-5174-a97f-f8394c0c5a98" :question/math-academy-id "q-81522" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071504/assets/fc474c9e41e73e04b3e4312e285726b9095a59f598016f6421943e0604d23abe.png)\n\nLet $U={1,2,3,a,b,c,d}$ be the universal set and let $W={3,b,c}.$ What is $\\overset{―}{W}?$" :question/worked-solution "The complement of $W,$ denoted $\\overset{―}{W},$ consists of all the elements in $U$ that are not in $W.$ To represent $\\overset{―}{W},$ we will shade in all the area of $U$ that is *outside* of $W,$ as follows:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071504/assets/365a6446a4ec6993447cf11190c8311027fac5bc9b0b36e85a4452fdfe85f7fa.png)\n\nThe elements in the shaded area are $1,2,a,$ and $d.$ These are the elements of $U$ that are not in $W.$ Therefore, the complement of $W$ is\n\n$$\n\\overset{―}{W}={1,2,a,d}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186371965 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "19fb3196-439e-5466-b50c-615c492167b4" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Complement of a Set Using a Venn Diagram"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f158ada4-ed14-56c5-a377-a4645658e92b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{1,2,3,4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186371967}